  ### Controlled verification

  Create a disposable named session. Inside it:

  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8080/ping
  export RECONNECT_PROBE=working
  cd /tmp
  echo $$

  The ping should report HealthyBusy.

  From another local terminal, find only the local AgentCore attachment process:

  pgrep -fl "agentcore exec"

  Terminate its exact PID:

  kill -TERM <PID>

  The first terminal should show Reconnecting (1/5) and return to the same shell. Verify:

  echo "$RECONNECT_PROBE"
  pwd
  echo $$

  Expect working, /tmp, and the same shell PID. This directly proves same-shell reconnection. AWS documents that reusing shellId preserves terminal state and buffered output. AWS interactive-shell documentation
  (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/runtime-get-started-command-shell.html)